<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine wheat bumper in south, shrivels in north.</title>
<headline>Argentine wheat bumper in south, shrivels in north.</headline>
<byline>Jason Webb</byline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's 1996/97 wheat crop badly needs water in the north, where the final sown area looks set to disappoint, but the grain belt's southern heart is enjoying excellent conditions, analysts and traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Some fields in Santa Fe and Cordoba are in very bad shape after the very high temperatures we had last week and then the near frost. That's bad for wheat, particularly when it's low on moisture,&quot; one private analyst said.</p>
</text>
